{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Pass through.</b> [As in] 'to your land, O daughter of Tarshish'; the meaning is: flee to your place quickly, like the flowing of the Nile. Or: pass through your land like the passing of the Nile." "<b>There is no girdle.</b> Like 'and girded with a מזח continually' (Psalms 109:19); a figure for a belt that strengthens the loins."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:47.963201019Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}